Modifications for DeepSeek Harness (Apache-2.0):
  - native DSH tools, slash commands, prompt section and embedded skills;
  - one Codex run per native DSH background job, streaming and cancellation;
  - Harness-approval gating for write-capable runs (writeApproval config);
  - typed refusals for app-server server-to-client requests;
  - session/data-dir plumbing, cross-process state locking, atomic writes;
  - shared broker creation lock, idle reaping, active-turn protection and
    turn/interrupt timeouts;
  - cancellation race fixes and recovery of orphaned turns;
  - untracked-symlink redaction in review context;
  - profile-independent state, `~` expansion, pinned resolved Codex executable;
  - Claude session-transfer command and Claude-specific hooks removed;
  - fixes for upstream issues in the vendored runtime: inline `--key=value`
    parsing (#807), git status column and quoted file names in review context
    (#813, #812), surrogate-safe thread names (#793), turn capture without a
    start-response turn id (#781), killing a broker that misses its readiness
    window (#801/#789), fatal `error` + `turn/completed` reported as failure
    (openai/codex#47728), and a total budget for inlined untracked files.
  See dsh-codex/NOTICE for the bundle-level list and docs/RESEARCH.md for details.

